post_install() {
    cat <<'MSG'
ReAgent is installed at /opt/reagent (a self-contained venv on Python 3.11).

Two one-time steps before the first plan:

  reagent-download-data ~/.local/share/reagent
  reagent build-stock-cache

The first pulls the pretrained USPTO expansion policy, the filter policy and
the ZINC stock, about 760 MB. The second hashes that stock so later runs need
roughly 0.6 GB of memory instead of 4.9 GB.

Then:

  reagent plan "CC(=O)Oc1ccccc1C(=O)O"

The agent layer is optional. It needs either a local Ollama server (--local)
or ANTHROPIC_API_KEY (--assess). Planning, features and evaluation run without
either.
MSG
}

post_upgrade() {
    cat <<'MSG'
The venv under /opt/reagent was rebuilt. Downloaded model data and stock caches
outside that directory are untouched.
MSG
}
